course: dictionary
lesson: 480
title: Arthritis: sore, stiff joints
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arthritis is an illness that makes the joints swollen, stiff and painful. A joint is the place where two bones meet, like your knee, hip or finger. The sentence «Many old dogs have stiff, sore joints called arthritis» gives the clue: the word called tells you that arthritis is the name for those stiff, sore joints.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «A chronic condition is an illness that lasts a long time or for life, like arthritis, asthma or heart disease» tells you that arthritis is an illness, and that it lasts a long time. The list of examples shows it is the same kind of thing as asthma and heart disease.
explain: Sayings are not always true. «Crack your knuckles and you'll get arthritis» is a rule passed from person to person. But the text tells you that one doctor cracked the knuckles of one hand for over sixty years and found no arthritis, and studies have not shown cracking to be harmful. Check a claim before you believe it, even if many people say it.
fact: Arthritis is an illness that makes joints swollen, stiff and painful.
fact: A joint is a place where two bones meet, like your knees, hips and fingers.
fact: Arthritis is a chronic condition: it lasts a long time or for life, and it can often be controlled but not cured.
fact: Arthritis is most common in older people, but children can get a kind of arthritis too.
fact: Exercise, medicine and keeping warm help people with arthritis.
exercise: «Many old dogs have stiff, sore joints called arthritis.» What is arthritis? | *An illness that makes joints swollen, stiff and painful | A short, gentle walk | A kind of soft bed for dogs | A sport played on the grass
exercise: Which of these is listed as an example of a chronic condition in «a chronic condition is an illness that lasts a long time or for life, like arthritis, asthma or heart disease»? | A sprained ankle | A cut knee | *Asthma | Measles
exercise: The sport saying says cracking knuckles gives you arthritis. What does the doctor's example show? | It proves the saying is true | It shows cracking knuckles breaks bones | *It shows the saying is not proven, because he found no arthritis after sixty years
test: Which three problems does arthritis cause in joints? | Light, bright and glowing | Hot, wet and grey | *Swollen, stiff and painful | Loud, fast and short
test: Why is a chronic condition hard to get rid of? | It spreads to the whole family | It lasts for a short time only | *It can often be controlled but not cured | It is cured in one day
exam: Which is true about arthritis? | Only grandparents can get it | *Children can get a kind of arthritis too | It makes joints glow in the dark | Cracking knuckles always causes it
